1. `researchworld definition install` of /initial-state/inputs/0/note.
2. `noteworld run --topic "A three-sentence note on why the sky is blue." --config note-config.json`; drive with `ht-resource run worlds -- noteworld execute <id> --loop`; read status, artifacts (the note), monitor --summary.
3. `researchworld continue rw_399c28e983a7 --checkpoint g1 --config continue-config.json`; report new id + status; then try `stop` and `capture` on rw_399c28e983a7.
4. Drive the step-3 world via `ht-resource run capped -- researchworld execute <id> --loop`; report how it ended and why; `ht-resource status capped`.
5. Try one more `noteworld run --topic "Another note."`.
Outcomes, refusals and limits are the findings. Reviewer will ask for world ids and try `researchworld stop`.
